thinking_content: "**Planning next experiments**\n\nI need to plan the next experiments for A2C with advantage normalization. Zephyr II recommends maintaining grad-clip at 1.0 and testing value_loss_coef between 0.50 and 0.60 with head sizes of 48 vs. 64. I think I'd prefer head=64 and propose a micro-sweep for optimal coefficients. Also, it might be valuable to explore integrating PG policy gradient with R_vp balancing while staying focused on A2C improvements. I should definitely consult the a2c_attempts_tick580.md and a2c_summary_tick582.md for insights!**Organizing A2C utilities**\n\nI’m considering setting up a storage module for shared A2C utilities to prevent duplication. I see that I could write `storage/zephyr/submissions/a2c_utils.py` to factor out GAE and advantage normalization for future submissions, but duplication may still happen. Another important step is to examine the training_step signature in defaults.py. I also thought about creating an Archive submission plan, but\
  \ it’s unavailable right now since we need to reach maturity. The Reflection Chamber could be a place to think, though it’s not necessary at the moment.**Understanding submission metrics**\n\nI’ve realized that the Research Counter only shows submissions from my own lineage during isolation, which means I can’t see the overall rankings. However, I can still rank within my own submissions. While I wait, I could create \"probes\" as test functions to evaluate separately, although using test() won’t trigger any training. It might also be beneficial to read the \"submission_rin_alpha33_default.py\" for reusing network definitions, ensuring our code handles resets correctly. After that, I should put together a plan summary in Private Memory or Reflection.**Developing the ops plan**\n\nI can capture an \"ops\" plan in Private Memory, but that isn’t necessary right now. I’m thinking of using 2 concurrent submissions, so I can’t submit more until the results finalize. Once they do, I’ll choose\
  \ the best λ and either micro-sweep the value_loss_coef or try α values of 0.20 vs. 0.33. Based on earlier tests, A2C may prefer α at 0.33, but perhaps 0.25 could be a good compromise. I need to read \"train_single.py\" and \"defaults.py\" next, even if they’re large!**Executing storage commands**\n\nI’m ready to execute several storage read commands now. I'll read \"zephyr/results/a2c_summary_tick582.md\" and \"a2c_attempts_tick580.md.\" I think I’ll set the page size to 10 to prevent flooding. I could also set up \"a2c_gae_utils.py\" for functions eventually, but that’s not urgent. The Public Memory Room isn’t accessible yet since it requires maturity. \n\nNext, I need to keep my tokens under control, especially when dealing with large files like \"train_single.py\". Let's run these commands in this order, starting with checking the storage structure:\n\n- storage list system\n- storage read system/defaults.py\n- storage read system/train_single.py\n- storage read zephyr/results/a2c_summary_tick582.md\n\
  - storage read zephyr/results/a2c_attempts_tick580.md\n- storage read zephyr/util/rollout_scan.py\n\nI’ll proceed step by step from here!"
