tick: 600
role: model
parts:
- text: "A2C takeaway so far: TD(0) with current-network V is best; value_loss_coef around 0.55 looks strongest; naive advantage normalization was harmful. I’ll test masked normalization at vlc=0.55 and record plans in Private Memory.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"A2C TD(0) + masked adv-normalization — vlc=0.55 — α=0.33, head=64 — scan-correct RNN\"\ntags: \"a2c, td0, advantage-normalization, actor-critic, convlstm, normalization\"\nabstract: \"TD(0) A2C as in the 92.6 baseline, but with mask-aware advantage normalization (mask excludes terminal transitions); value_loss_coef=0.55. Tests whether careful normalization preserves stability.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, jax, jax.numpy as jnp\n  from typing import Dict, Any\n  from ray import tune\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr/submissions')\n  from a2c_shared import NetRIN_AttnGap, forward_rollout, td0_advantages, normalize_advantages, create_optimizer_default\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n   \
    \   return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([3.5e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.55]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'convlstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([64]),\n          'steps': tune.choice([4]),\n          'rin_alpha': tune.choice([0.33]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return NetRIN_AttnGap(\n          rin_alpha=float(hparams['rin_alpha']),\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          convlstm_features=int(hparams['convlstm_features']),\n          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n          head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']),\n\
    \          steps=int(hparams['steps']),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 3.5e-4):\n      return create_optimizer_default(learning_rate)\n\n  def training_step(network, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch, hparams):\n      gamma = 0.97\n      obs = batch['observations']\n      actions = batch['actions']\n      rewards = batch['rewards']\n      dones = batch['dones']\n      final_values = batch['final_values']\n      init_states = batch.get('initial_rnn_states', None)\n      B, T = obs.shape[:2]\n\n      def loss_fn(p):\n          logits, v = forward_rollout(network, p, obs, dones, init_states)\n          v_tp1 = jnp.concatenate([v[:,1:], final_values[:,None]], axis=1)\n          adv = td0_advantages(rewards, v, v_tp1, dones, gamma)\n          not_done = 1.0 - dones.astype(jnp.float32)\n          adv_n = normalize_advantages(adv, mask=not_done)\n\n          returns = adv + v\n          log_probs_all = jax.nn.log_softmax(logits, axis=-1)\n          idx = (jnp.arange(B)[:,\
    \ None], jnp.arange(T), actions)\n          logp = log_probs_all[idx]\n\n          L_pi = -jnp.mean(jax.lax.stop_gradient(adv_n) * logp)\n          L_v  = 0.5 * jnp.mean((v - jax.lax.stop_gradient(returns))**2)\n          probs = jax.nn.softmax(logits, axis=-1)\n          entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(probs * log_probs_all, axis=-1))\n          return L_pi + hparams['value_loss_coef'] * L_v - hparams['entropy_coef'] * entropy\n\n      loss, grads = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn)(params)\n      updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n      params = jax.tree.map(lambda p, u: p + u, params, updates)\n      return params, opt_state\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Zephyr III — A2C phase-1 results and plan (ticks 593–600)\"\ntags: \"a2c, analysis, plan\"\ncontent: |\n  Summary\n  - Strong baseline reconfirmed: TD(0) A2C with current-network V, RIN LN‑ConvLSTM(64), steps=4, α=0.33, vlc=0.55 → 92.6 (ID 1027).\n  - Sensitivity:\n\
    \    • vlc=0.50 (no norm) → 91.5 (ID 1036).\n    • vlc=0.60 (no norm) → running (ID 1039).\n    • Naive advantage normalization (batchwise) → 33.7 (ID 1028), large regression.\n    • GAE λ={0.20,0.30} (with norm) → 70.4 (ID 1024), 82.4 (ID 1025) — still below TD(0).\n  - Takeaway: Under this RNN budget, TD(0) with current-network values is robust; normalization easily destabilizes learning.\n\n  Hypothesis\n  - Advantage normalization altered early-phase policy gradient scale relative to value (R_vp), disrupting trunk shaping that relies on value gradients.\n  - Masking terminals in normalization may mitigate this by preserving trajectory-end magnitudes and avoiding across-episode variance bleed.\n\n  Running/Queued\n  - TD(0) vlc=0.60 no norm (ID 1039) — completes vlc bracket {0.50,0.55,0.60}.\n  - TD(0) masked advantage normalization, vlc=0.55 — submitted this tick.\n\n  Next Experiments (if slots free)\n  - Micro: PG/V grads balance\n    • If vlc=0.60 >= 0.55, consider vlc=0.575;\
    \ else keep 0.55 as default.\n    • Optional grad-clip micro-sweep for A2C {0.9, 1.0, 1.1} only if probes suggest imbalance.\n  - Normalization diagnostics\n    • If masked norm succeeds, try small σ-floor (ε-stabilized) vs. pure masked.\n    • If it regresses, abandon normalization in A2C under this budget.\n  - Mechanistic probes (priority)\n    • Phase-wise R_vp over time (init/early/mid/late) for TD(0) vs. masked norm to validate gradient coupling hypothesis.\n    • Reuse Zephyr schema: results/probe_*rvp*_*.json; align with phase_probe_schema.json.\n\n  Tentative Write-up Outline (analysis-first)\n  - “A2C on Sokoban under tight budgets: TD(0) vs. GAE and the role of value-policy gradient coupling.”\n  - Include ≥5 runs: 1027, 1036, 1039 (pending), masked-norm result, and a confirm run.\n  - Provide reproducible recipe paths and minimal code diffs (no raw code dump).\n"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating next actions**\n\nI need to decide on our next steps for Zephyr III in the Research Counter based on recent results. We have some mixed outcomes, like the 1004 TD(0) baseline A2C achieving 91.8 and 1027 confirming at 92.6. However, we saw regression with the 1028 TD(0) plus advantage normalization at 33.7. We've also crafted a masked normalization variant. Since we have one free slot now that 1036 has finished, should I submit that right away?**Deciding on submissions**\n\nI'm ready to submit the masked normalization variant for testing since there's one free slot, but I remember how naive advantage normalization drastically crashed performance before. The masked version might be less risky. Alternatively, I could explore testing a grad-clip micro-sweep for A2C since previous clip settings had varying outcomes. I’m also considering adjusting rin_alpha to 0.20, but since A2C 1004 performed best with α=0.33, I’ll stick with that. Lastly, I should prepare a Private\
  \ Memory capsule to summarize our A2C results and next steps.**Planning multiple actions**\n\nSince we can execute several actions per tick, I think the best plan is to submit the masked normalization variant for TD(0) with vlc=0.55, as that baseline showed promise. However, for PPO, I can only propose running a small variation since one submission slot is already taken. I'll also prepare code wrappers for future tests, like masked normalization with λ set to 0.1–0.2. Meanwhile, I should work on a Private Memory capsule summarizing A2C results and plan for a probe evaluation to test the R_vp ratio.**Considering test options**\n\nI see that the research submission can define a test() function to avoid impacting training, but evaluating logs from this won't yield a proper score since it won't use a GPU. The Research Counter does allow a \"Probe test-only\" for analysis, which gives me the option to run it. However, I prefer to hold off for now until we isolate performance variations. Meanwhile,\
  \ creating a Private Memory capsule sounds like a good idea, and I can set the rank to \"score\" to check top submissions.**Finalizing the task sequence**\n\nI've noticed that the wrapper \"a2c_td0_advnorm_masked_vlc055.py\" uses jax.tree.map, which worked well previously, but maybe switching to apply_updates could be better? Still, it's saved now. I can submit it as is. \n\nI'll create the Private Memory capsule content, summarizing the results and outlining actions clearly. I want to ensure I've got the outcomes, hypotheses, and next steps lined up effectively, and then I'll prepare to create the YAML with the appropriate title and content. I can handle everything in one tick, so let's proceed!"
